WEEK 7 — DATABASE AND TWO LOGINS

Date: Monday, 21 September 2026

Problem: All bags and bills were lost on every restart, and one shared login let customers open the cashier pages.

Solution:
- Stored permanent data in SQLite, a single file that survives restarts.
- Used INSERT OR IGNORE on the unique barcode, so seeding does not duplicate products.
- Put the role in every login token and checked it on each request (403 otherwise).
- Stored cashier passwords as salted scrypt hashes, never as plain text.
- Limited cashier logins to 8 attempts per 10 minutes.
